    Declare tqdm + langchain-core, drop nine unused dependencies
    
    Two direct imports were never declared and only resolved transitively, which
    made them silent time bombs: implementation/ingest.py imports tqdm (reached in
    production by refresh_kb.py -> implementation.ingest, so the weekly Actions run
    depended on it) and implementation/answer.py imports langchain_core.messages
    (reached by app.py, so it's in the image). tqdm arrived via gradio and
    huggingface-hub, langchain_core via langchain-google-genai. Removing the unused
    packages below would have broken the first one outright -- declaring both
    explicitly is what makes that cleanup safe.
    
    Removed as imported by nothing at all: langchain-openai, langchain-huggingface,
    langchain-community, langchain-text-splitters, openai, tiktoken, nbformat, and
    google-genai (the code reaches Gemini through langchain-google-genai, which
    still pulls google-genai itself). These were leftovers from the tutorial
    scaffold the project started from.
    
    langchain-chroma was also unused as an import -- it was only present to pull in
    chromadb, which two non-production scripts do import directly. So chromadb is
    now a dev dependency, declared as what's actually imported. Both workflows and
    the Dockerfile install with --no-dev, so it no longer reaches production at all.
    
    Net: 174 -> 159 resolved packages, and a smaller image.
    
    Verified against the production install (uv sync --frozen --no-dev, exactly what
    CI and Docker do): app, refresh_kb, visualize_embeddings, all three
    implementation modules and both scraper modules import cleanly, and
    tests/test_refresh_kb.py + tests/test_app.py are 26/26.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

